{
  "id": "27838_hiku",
  "headword": "{惹|ひ}く",
  "reading": "ひく",
  "romaji": "hiku",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to attract; to draw; to captivate",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to attract; to draw (interest, attention); to captivate",
      "explanation": "To draw someone's interest, attention, or feelings toward something. Written {惹|ひ}く specifically for attracting attention or the heart, distinguishing it from the general verb {引|ひ}く."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27838_hiku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{人|ひと}の{目|め}を{惹|ひ}く。",
      "english": "It catches people's eye.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27838_hiku_ex2",
      "japanese": "その{話|はなし}は{私|わたし}の{興味|きょうみ}を{惹|ひ}いた。",
      "english": "That story drew my interest.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27838_hiku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}の{明|あか}るい{笑顔|えがお}が、{多|おお}くの{人|ひと}の{心|こころ}を{惹|ひ}きつけた。",
      "english": "Her bright smile captivated the hearts of many people.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A meaning-specific spelling of {引|ひ}く used only for attracting attention, interest, or the heart. For all other senses (to pull, to subtract, to look up), {引|ひ}く is used.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {興味|きょうみ}を{惹|ひ}く: to attract interest\n- {人目|ひとめ}を{惹|ひ}く: to catch people's attention\n- {心|こころ}を{惹|ひ}かれる: to be drawn to / charmed by\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {引|ひ}く: to pull; to draw — the general verb; {惹|ひ}く is reserved for drawing interest or affection",
